{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesYaHs8RUVrXcSxhiabu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n## Requirement (restated)\nAdd a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED`, idempotently handles already-confirmed shipments, rejects cancelled shipments with 409, and returns 404 for missing shipments.\n\n## Repository findings\n\n**Shipment model** (`sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27`): Shipment data class has the required statuses (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED).\n\n**Controller** (`sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56`): Handles POST /shipments (create) and GET endpoints; no confirm endpoint exists.\n\n**Repository** (`sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`): InMemoryShipmentRepository provides save, existsById, findById, and findAll operations.\n\n**Exception hierarchy** (`sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:11-30`): Provides ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409).\n\n**Error codes** (`sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`): Current enum has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED; no code for invalid status transitions yet.\n\n**Exception handler** (`sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28`): Centralized handler maps ApiExceptions to ResponseEntity with ApiError envelope.\n\n## Conventions in repository\n\n- Controllers throw ApiExceptions rather than building response bodies\n- POST endpoints that succeed return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(...)\n- Read endpoints (GET) return the entity directly or throw ResourceNotFoundException\n- Error responses always use the ApiError envelope with error.code, error.message, error.fields\n- Tests assert both status codes and error.code values\n- Repository operations are injected and managed through @Repository\n- In-memory storage uses ConcurrentHashMap\n\n## Affected files\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Must add SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED error code (or similar)\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Must add tests for confirm endpoint (4 cases: created→confirmed, idempotent confirm, cancelled rejection, missing id)\n\n## Risks\n\n- The requirement says \"confirming already CONFIRMED succeeds and changes nothing\"; the question is whether this returns 200 OK or 201 Created. Convention from POST suggests 200 OK (idempotent success), not 201.\n- Updating an existing Shipment requires modifying a copy (data classes are immutable); the repository's save() method handles this via map reassignment.\n- If a concurrent confirm attempt happens while another is in flight on the same shipment, the in-memory ConcurrentHashMap should handle it safely but no locking is in place (acceptable for a benchmark fixture).\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. **HTTP status for idempotent confirm**: Should a repeated confirm return 200 OK or 201 Created? The spec says \"succeeds and changes nothing\" but does not name the status. Looking at REST conventions and the ticket context (\"Operations retries this call\"), 200 OK is the standard for idempotent updates that don't create new resources.\n\n2. **Error code for invalid transition**: The spec says confirming a CANCELLED shipment is \"rejected with 409\", but doesn't name an error code. Should this use an existing code like SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS or a new code like SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED? The existing pattern (SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS for duplicate IDs) suggests a specific code per scenario; a new code is clearer.\n\n**Recommendation**: Proceed assuming 200 OK for successful confirms (both first and retry), and add a new ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED for the 409 case.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n## Proposed changes\n\n**1. ApiError.kt** — Add a new error code:\n- Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum to signal when a confirm is attempted on a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n**2. ShipmentController.kt** — Add confirm endpoint:\n- Add a new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>` annotated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`.\n- Logic:\n  - Find the shipment by ID; throw ResourceNotFoundException if missing.\n  - If status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED, save, return ResponseEntity.ok(saved).\n  - If status is CONFIRMED, return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) (idempotent, no update needed).\n  - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED.\n\n**3. ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test methods:\n- `confirmCreatedShipmentTransitionsToConfirmed()` — create S-1 in CREATED, confirm it, assert it transitions to CONFIRMED and returns 200 OK.\n- `confirmAlreadyConfirmedShipmentIdempotent()` — create S-2, confirm twice, assert both return 200 OK and status remains CONFIRMED.\n- `confirmCancelledShipmentRejected()` — create S-3, manually set it to CANCELLED in the repository, attempt confirm, assert 409 with error code SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED.\n- `confirmNonexistentShipmentNotFound()` — attempt confirm on S-missing, assert 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND.\n\n## Alternatives considered and rejected\n\n**Alternative 1: Add a `ConfirmShipmentRequest` data class**\n- **Rejected** because the confirm operation takes no input payload; accepting an empty body is awkward and the endpoint's identity is already established by the shipmentId path variable.\n\n**Alternative 2: Create a separate ShipmentService class**\n- **Rejected** because existing controllers (ShipmentController, OrderController) handle logic directly without a service layer; adding one would break the established convention and increase scope.\n\n**Alternative 3: Use a PATCH endpoint instead of POST**\n- **Rejected** because the ticket explicitly names POST, and POST is idiomatic for state transitions (confirm, publish, etc.) in REST APIs.\n\n**Alternative 4: Add a new ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION**\n- **Rejected** in favor of SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED because it is more specific and clearer for clients; the ticket describes one specific rejection case (CANCELLED), not a general state machine violation.\n\n## Data and error flow\n\n**Case 1: Confirm a CREATED shipment**\n- Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (no body)\n- Controller: Finds S-1, reads status=CREATED\n- Action: Creates new Shipment with status=CONFIRMED, calls repository.save()\n- Response: 200 OK with updated Shipment in body\n- Written: Shipment with new status in repository\n\n**Case 2: Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment (retry)**\n- Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (no body)\n- Controller: Finds S-1, reads status=CONFIRMED\n- Action: Returns existing shipment without update\n- Response: 200 OK with unchanged Shipment in body\n- Written: Nothing (idempotent)\n\n**Case 3: Confirm a CANCELLED shipment**\n- Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (no body)\n- Controller: Finds S-1, reads status=CANCELLED\n- Action: Throws ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED, \"...\")\n- Response: 409 Conflict with ApiError envelope containing error.code=SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED\n- Written: Nothing\n\n**Case 4: Confirm a non-existent shipment**\n- Request: POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm (no body)\n- Controller: repository.findById() returns null\n- Action: Throws ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, \"...\")\n- Response: 404 Not Found with ApiError envelope containing error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n- Written: Nothing\n\n## Test strategy\n\n1. **confirmCreatedShipmentTransitionsToConfirmed** — Validates primary success path: CREATED → CONFIRMED\n2. **confirmAlreadyConfirmedShipmentIdempotent** — Validates idempotency: repeated confirm on CONFIRMED succeeds\n3. **confirmCancelledShipmentRejected** — Validates business rule: CANCELLED cannot be confirmed (409)\n4. **confirmNonexistentShipmentNotFound** — Validates error case: missing shipment returns 404\n\nEach test uses the same MockMvc integration test pattern as existing tests, and asserts both status code and error.code in error cases.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1466,"cache_read_input_tokens":16317,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1466},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8936c5ce-4d14-4bcc-8b7d-229339184734","uuid":"61b7a6d3-eddd-46bd-9951-d93626fdac23","timestamp":"2026-09-09T08:25:08.607Z","request_id":"req_011CesYaH1HaZncRdF1bhVoa"}
